        "original_id": "6dd223ed-5372-5cd4-a4df-885b5e1af657",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Walkley Heights, South Australia; Yatala Labour Prison\n- People: R. M. Williams; Sir Thomas Playford\n- Topics: prison farm land; compulsory land acquisition; prison construction; quarrying for roads and construction\n\nFacts:\n- Yatala Labour Prison was built in 1854 to enable prisoners to work at the creek quarrying rock for roads and construction.\n- Walkley Heights, South Australia, is located on land that formerly comprised the prison farm for Yatala Labour Prison.\n- Walkley Heights, South Australia, includes fifty-five hectares of land formerly owned by R. M. Williams that was compulsorily acquired during the time of former State Premier Sir Thomas Playford.",
